# Class: obo:PROMOT_1200001 (Doble anomalía del potencial de acción motora compuesta)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:PROMOT_1200001 "The double compound muscle action potential (CMAP) or double “M wave” is a recording from a muscle as a result of motor nerve stimulation. It is a duplication of the fundamental signal in motor nerve conduction and related studies (e.g., F waves, H reflex, repetitive motor nerve stimulation, etc.). It is a double banal, simple waveform observable through instrumentation. "@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000119 "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11131082/") rdfs:comment obo:PROMOT_1200001 "(JP : to validate)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PROMOT_1200001 "Doble anomalía del potencial de acción motora compuesta"@es)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PROMOT_1200001 "Double compound motor action potential abnormality"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:PROMOT_1200001 obo:HP_0033580)

